      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A mathematical model of age mortality due to coronary heart disease among populations of the 24 European countries was made on the basis of the principal components method. It was shown that age and sex differences of mortality can be described by means of three different factors which are statistically independent on each other. Possible pathogenetic mechanisms underlying the formation of the three factors are discussed."},
